From 9fde803e81db2bbdb40952a2b253c7225b4e31a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DarkSharpness <2040703891@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:30:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] [DSv4.1] Write the prefill top-k straight into the raw
 selection

The DeepGEMM prefill top-k now writes request-local compressed positions
into the raw-index buffer that sparse prefill reads, instead of flattened
columns that write_selection sorted and mapped back. Pool slots are only
derived when this forward's attention reads them (trtllm, non-sparse
extend, late-layer tail, request window). The Selection struct is gone:
the selection buffers are fields of PrefillInputs / DecodeInputs /
CapturedPrefillInputs. write_selection keeps only the CP dense-blocks path
and no longer sorts. Per index layer at 8192 tokens on B200: 466 -> 184 us
(full top-k), 523 -> 219 us (candidate consumer).

test_dense_prefill_indexer and test_dsv4_nonpaged_indexer still use the
old signatures and need an update.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
