From 3814a5cc1550b2820f9db08821ece4f217413ff2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DarkSharpness <2040703891@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:09:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] [DSv4.1] Pin the row-pair id contract for the sparse
 schedule

The pairing is only correct because DeepGEMM's paged scheduler has
BLOCK_Q == 2: the ids delimit what it already groups, and its page table is
indexed by Q row rather than by the id value. That lived in the commit
message, where a later BLOCK_Q change would not find it; state it on
_row_pair_ids instead.

Cover it too. The existing cases are single-request, so nothing saw a pair
spanning two requests. Schedule the same rows twice, once with the row-pair
ids and once with the per-request ids they replaced, and require the same
paged sparse logits over each row's valid length, for requests with odd row
counts and for the single-row and zero-row degenerate groups. Pairing
globally instead of per request fails only this case.

Also take a tail that starts on the odd half of a pair, which the existing
tail case does not: tail() slices the id vector rather than rebuilding it,
so that row is left a group of one. Asserted on the selection's shape and
membership in the row's published blocks, not on overlap with the full
table, since the two row sets pair differently.

Validated on 1x B200 with sgl_deep_gemm 0.2.1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
